@*
    The empire's own settings, as distinct from its species'. A human empire is not called "Human",
    and the two are changed independently, so they sit in different places.

    Three things, each its own component: what the empire is called, which scripted country flags it
    claims, and whether it may turn up in somebody else's game. They are components because the lite
    card reaches for them one at a time — it names an empire by pressing its name, and cycles the
    spawn setting on the card itself — and one editor per thing is what keeps the two shells from
    disagreeing about any of them.
*@

